Potential issue in world.js `createSim` uses `eye` etc fine.

Neighborhood constructor calls build() which calls setProgress() at end. `buildNpc` marker push. setProgress iterates houses refresh. Fine.

Ground `g.position.y` default 0.03 for sim? Use 0.02.

Now write game.js with ~900 lines.

Let me carefully define all DOM refs.

```js
const el = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
const ui = {
 title: el('title-screen'), start: el('start-btn'), ...
}
```

Scene init:
```
