renderer.toneMapping = THREE.ACESFilmicToneMapping;
renderer.toneMappingExposure = 1.12;
renderer.outputColorSpace = THREE.SRGBColorSpace;
```

Neighborhood camera: PerspectiveCamera(48, aspect, 0.1, 400).

Set initial camera:
```
let camYaw=0, camPitch=0.64, camDist=16;
camN.position.set(0,17,36);
```

`neighborhood.updateMarkers` uses camera; after camera update.

Title markers hidden via style.

Player state:
```
const player = { pos: neighborhood.getSpawn(), y: 0.3, angle:0, moveSpeed:0 };
const sim = createSim(...);
sim.group.position.copy(player.pos);
sceneN.add(sim.group);
```
`neighborhood.getSpawn()` returns y=0 pos; set y computed.

groundHeight:
```
function groundHeight(x,z){ return Math.hypot(x,z) < 10.35 ? 0.3 : 0.02; }
```
Spawn at 7.6 radius <10.35 => 0.3 (island). Good.

Player sim group y = groundHeight.

Update input:
```
function syncInput(){
 const k = keys;
 const kf = (k.has('KeyW')||k.has('ArrowUp')?1:0) - (k.has('KeyS')||k.has('ArrowDown')?1:0);
 const kr = (k.has('KeyD')||k.has('ArrowRight')?1:0) - (k.has('KeyA')||k.has('ArrowLeft')?1:0);
 input.forward = clamp(kf + touchMove.f, -1,1);
 input.right = clamp(kr + touchMove.r, -1,1);
 input.sprint = k.has('ShiftLeft')||k.has('ShiftRight');
}
```
For LevelRun, movement uses input.forward/right and level's yaw. Fine.

Touch joystick sets touchMove.

`updatePlayer(dt)`:
```
if (dialogue open || mapOpen) { input.forward=0...; sim.update idle; return; }
syncInput();
const f = input.forward, r = input.right; len...
const speed = (input.sprint?8.4:5.4);
const sy=Math.sin(camYaw), cy=Math.cos(camYaw);
let dx = (-sy*f + cy*r), dz=(-cy*f - sy*r);
normalize if len>1;
player.pos.x += dx*speed*dt; ...
resolveColliders(player.pos, 0.5, neighborhood.colliders);
// boundary
const rad=Math.hypot(x,z); if(rad>46){scale}
player.y = lerp...
```
Update sim:
```
const moving = len>0.05;
sim.update(dt, moving && !dialogue, speed/5.4);
sim.group.position.set(pos.x, player.y, pos.z);
if moving, targetAngle=atan2(dx,dz); smooth angle difference.
```
Note sim walk speed argument.

`updateNeighborhoodCamera(dt, titled)`:
```
const target = new THREE.Vector3(player.pos.x, player.y+1.35, player.pos.z);
let desiredX...
if state==='title' or 'ending'? use orbit.
```
Ending maybe orbit too. For intro, keep follow? Intro overlay over neighborhood; camera can stay follow.

Implement:
```
if (G.state==='title') {
  const a = 0.4 + Math.sin(t*0.035)*0.35;
  desired.set(Math.sin(a)*33, 19 + Math.sin(t*0.1)*0.8, Math.cos(a)*33);
