Title in landscape: top of "WHISPERING" clipped (the logo top off-screen), bottom title foot visible. No kicker; probably top clipped. Need fix.

Design a landscape media query. Let's target `@media (max-height: 520px) and (orientation: landscape)` regardless width, since touch landscape. But desktop small windows also benefit. We can use `@media (max-height: 520px)` only.

Adjustments:
1. Title:
```
.title-screen { justify-content:center; padding: 10px 24px; }
.title-inner { transform? } 
.logo { margin-top:6px; }
.logo-top { font-size: clamp(22px, 5vw, 40px); }
.logo-bottom { font-size: clamp(52px, 15vw, 100px); }
.title-rule { margin: 10px auto 8px; }
.tagline { font-size: 14px; }
.blurb { display:none; }
#start-btn { margin-top: 12px; padding: 12px; }
.title-meta { display:none; }
.title-foot { margin-top: 10px; }
.title-scroll { display:none; }
```
At 844 width: logo top 42, bottom 100; total ~150; kicker 9; rule 20; tagline 20; button 48; foot 20 => ~280 fits 390. Good.

2. In landscape touch layout:
- `#touch .touch-right { flex-direction: row; align-items: flex-end; gap: 8px; bottom: calc(72px + safe); }` but in level bottom must be above HUD (66): 74. In neighborhood bottom 20 could be fine, but consistent 74 puts buttons higher; okay.
- Sizes: fire 64, use 46, swap 38. map 38.
- Row order: swap, use, fire (order values still). For neighborhood map, use: map (order1), use (order2). So row would show MAP then USE left-to-right, ending with USE at right edge. Fine.
- This row width ~38+46+64+16=164, right 18 => x 662..826, y 248..312; no minimap overlap (minimap ends 150).
- But in level, HUD y324..390; row bottom 72 => y 390-72-64=254..318. Good.
- Minimap/obj panel could stay. Pause top 160 no overlap.
- Doom HUD stats: height 66, stats fit width 844 easily. Fine.
- Minimap is 108 CSS at right top; okay.
